course: dictionary
lesson: 10916
title: Voice: a sound, and a say
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «The voice tells you who someone is.» Here voice means the sound a person makes, because a voice is how you know who is speaking. Try the meaning in the sentence to check that it fits.
explain: «... her voice dies away» in the Alice story means her voice gets quieter and quieter until you cannot hear it. A voice can be loud, quiet, high, low, kind or angry, and the words around it give clues. Look for words like whispering, booming or shaking.
explain: Voice has a second meaning too. Having a voice means having the right to say what you think, and to voice an opinion means to say it out loud. So when someone says every child should have a voice, they mean every child should be able to share their ideas.
explain: Phrases help as well: lose your voice (you can no longer speak properly), raise your voice (speak louder), lower your voice (speak more quietly). When you meet voice, ask which meaning fits the sentence best.
fact: Your voice is the sound you make when you speak or sing.
fact: Voice can be a noun (a voice) or a verb: to voice an opinion means to say it.
fact: Having a voice means having the right to say what you think.
fact: Inside voices are quiet, and outside voices are loud.
fact: Your voice is made by vocal cords in your throat, which vibrate when air passes through them.
exercise: «The voice tells you who someone is.» In this sentence, what is a voice? | A kind of musical instrument | *A sound a person makes when they speak or sing | A room where people sit quietly | A loud argument
exercise: «... her voice dies away.» What does dies away mean here? | Moves to another room | Gets louder and louder | *Gets quieter until you cannot hear it | Changes into a different language
exercise: Mia says every child should have a voice in class. What does having a voice mean? | Being able to sing very high | Having a loud cough | *Having the right to say what you think | Being the tallest in the class
test: When Sam says he will voice his opinion, what does he mean? | *He will say what he thinks | He will go quiet for the day | He will write a poem about pigs | He will keep his ideas secret
test: Which phrase means to speak more quietly? | *Lower your voice | Voice your opinion | Raise your voice | Lose your voice
exam: «The posh voice can make the baddie seem cold and powerful.» In this sentence, voice means | A type of bird | *The way a character sounds when they speak | A loud shout only | A vote in an election
